We need origin_node_ready and destination_node_ready true at time of assembling leg. We can achieve ready via activate_origin_node and activate_destination_node (which require candidate_prepared, task profile linked, node linked, not ready, not occupied). However after we load cargo, origin_node_occupied becomes true, which would block activate_origin_node precondition (requires not occupied). So we must activate before loading cargo (since activate requires not occupied). Similarly for destination.

Thus order: For each availability, we need to:

- Ensure candidate_prepared (we will do via attach task profile and confirm preparedness)
- Activate node (makes ready)
- Load cargo (makes occupied, locked, payload link, cargo not available)
- Unload cargo (makes confirmed true, cargo available, removes payload link, keeps occupied and locked)
- Then we have node occupied and ready, locked and confirmed, cargo available again, payload link false.

Now we need to link transport leg to origin and destination nodes (transport_leg_origin_linked and transport_leg_destination_linked) and have transport_leg_assembled and loading authorized.

We can assemble transport leg after origin and destination availability are locked (since assemble actions require origin_availability_locked and destination_availability_locked). Also need origin_node_ready and destination_node_ready (we have after load/unload? Let's see: after load, origin_node_occupied true; after unload, origin_node_ready true (set by unload). So we have both occupied and ready. Good. Also need origin_availability_confirmed true (we have after unload). Destination similarly.

Thus after we have both origin and destination availability locked and confirmed, we can assemble transport leg.

Which assemble action to use? We need transport_leg_assembled, origin_leg_loaded? Not required for goal. Goal only requires transport_leg_assembled, origin_linked, destination_linked, loading_authorized. It does not require origin_leg_loaded or destination_leg_loaded. So we can use assemble_transport_leg (basic) which requires origin_availability_locked, destination_availability_locked, origin_node_ready, destination_node_ready, origin_availability_confirmed, destination_availability_confirmed, transport_leg_available. Effects: transport_leg_assembled, origin_linked, destination_linked, not transport_leg_available.

Thus we can use assemble_transport_leg after we have locked and confirmed both availabilities.

Then we need transport_leg_loading_authorized. Action authorize_transport_leg_loading: parameters (?transport_leg - transport_leg ?origin_availability - origin_candidate_availability ?route_task_profile - route_task_profile). Precondition: transport_leg_assembled ?transport_leg, origin_availability_locked ?origin_availability, candidate_task_profile_linked ?origin_availability ?route_task_profile, not transport_leg_loading_authorized ?transport_letter. Effect: transport_leg_loading_authorized ?transport_leg.

